        question: "Do engineers charge per sheet or a flat fee for stamping?",
        answer: "Flat fee by scope is standard — the fee follows building type, size, wind exposure, and soil complexity. Oklahoma's wind detailing means a small sheet count can still carry heavy engineering, so per-sheet pricing would misprice the work. Get the flat fee and its inclusions in writing, especially how plan-check corrections are billed, since wind-detail comments are common.",
